{"id": "49e67b78-6468-4de2-b909-a4ccc852c975", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Error 0x80070422 happens when the Windows Update service itself is disabled, so Windows can't even start it to check for updates. This is a known issue with a clear fix—I should guide them through re-enabling the wuauserv service rather than treating it as a mystery to diagnose.

I should check the same disabled/startup-type issue for BITS and the registry Start values under wuauserv, plus look for GPO settings like NoAutoUpdate or WSUS misconfiguration (UseWUServer pointing somewhere unreachable) that could be blocking updates. After fixing services, I'd rerun the patch baseline scan via Run Command and check the output, noting that if the service gets disabled again it likely points to a hardening script, GPO, or security tool reapplying the setting on a CIS-hardened AMI.

